        "original_id": "de4a83d5-b1f9-5f28-94b4-da1253b4ca6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jamal Igle, Geoff Johns, James Robinson, Sterling Gates, Gary Frank, Alex Ross, Renato Guedes, Pete Woods\n- Characters: Firestorm, Killer Frost, Supergirl\n- Comics: Molly Danger, Superman: New Krypton\n- Companies: DC Comics\n- Organizations: Justice League of America\n- Events: DC Rebirth\n\nFacts:\n- Jamal Igle created the comic book series Molly Danger.\n- Jamal Igle is known for pencilling, inking, and coloring work on Supergirl and Firestorm.\n- Firestorm is the name of several fictional superheroes appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics.\n- Superman: New Krypton is a 2008–2009 Superman story arc published by DC Comics.\n- Superman: New Krypton was written by Geoff Johns, James Robinson, and Sterling Gates.\n- Superman: New Krypton featured art by Gary Frank, Alex Ross, Renato Guedes, Jamal Igle, and Pete Woods.\n- Killer Frost formerly appeared as an adversary of the superhero Firestorm.\n- In 2016, DC Rebirth started a new Justice League of America, and Killer Frost became a member of that team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3151b5a9-c5d0-5d1c-a0f6-e73aba970075",
        "text": "Page: Jamal Igle. Sentence: The creator of the comic book series Molly Danger he is also known for his pencilling, inking and coloring work on books such as \"Supergirl\" and \"Firestorm\".\nPage: Firestorm (comics). Sentence: Firestorm is the name of several fictional superheroes appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics.\nPage: Superman: New Krypton. Sentence: \"New Krypton\" is a 2008-2009 Superman story arc written by Geoff Johns, James Robinson, and Sterling Gates with art by Gary Frank, Alex Ross, Renato Guedes, Jamal Igle and Pete Woods and published by DC Comics.\nPage: Killer Frost. Sentence: Killer Frost appeared formerly as an adversary of the superhero Firestorm but is now a member of the new Justice League of America that started with the DC Rebirth in 2016.",
